    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113">

                <pb facs="0160" n="150" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg150"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3–1348: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-03-13T17:00:00+08:00">March 13, 1948—5
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 13—7:36 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>463. Chinese newspaperwoman, regarded as reliable, informs us that in recent
                    unofficial conversations with Shanghai Communist representatives on subject
                    coalition government, they stated that they would not negotiate with any Chinese
                    government led by Generalissimo. On March 11 Lo Lung-chi<anchor n="27"
                        xml:id="d113-f1"/> informed officer of Embassy to same effect, namely, that
                    Communists have refused to negotiate with any government in which Gimo and
                    certain of his closest supporters participate. Lo also stated categorically that
                    Gimo now favors negotiating settlement with Communists and implied that Gimo had
                    sanctioned informal exploratory advances by certain unnamed members of
                    Government for this purpose. Memo of conversation with Lo Lung-chi this subject
                    forwarded under cover Embdes 124, March 12.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d113-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d113-f1" n="27" xml:id="d113-f1-content">
                <p>Leader of the former Democratic League.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d113-f2" n="28" xml:id="d113-f2-content">
